<title>USA: U.S. Oct import prices rose 0.4 pct.</title>
<headline>U.S. Oct import prices rose 0.4 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Labor Department report of U.S. import and export price changes by percent (unadjusted).</p>
<p>    -			   Oct   Sept-Rev from  Oct 96/95</p>
<p> ALL IMPORTS		  0.4    1.1    0.8	1.8</p>
<p> -Petroleum		   6.1    7.4    5.0     37.6</p>
<p> -Nonpetroleum	     -0.3    0.3    0.3     -1.6</p>
<p> -Food, Feed, Drink	 0.1    1.9    1.9	0.1</p>
<p> -Industrial Supplies     2.0    3.0    2.3	9.2</p>
<p> -Capital Goods	    -0.3   -0.1   -0.1     -3.0</p>
<p> -Motor Vehicles,Parts   -0.3    0.3    0.3     -0.2</p>
<p> -Consumer Goods ExAutos -0.2    0.2    0.2	0.1</p>
<p>Percent changes, not seasonally adjusted --</p>
<p> ALL EXPORTS		 -0.3   -0.8   -0.8     -1.0</p>
<p> -Agricultural	     -2.7   -7.2   -7.3     -1.0</p>
<p> -Non-Agricultural	  0.1    0.1    0.1     -0.9</p>
<p> -Food, Feed, Drink	-3.0   -8.5   -8.5     -1.6</p>
<p> -Industrial Supplies     0.3    0.6    0.6     -3.3</p>
<p> -Capital Goods	    UNCH   -0.2   -0.1     UNCH</p>
<p> -Motor Vehicles,Parts    0.2    UNCH  UNCH	0.5</p>
<p> -Consumer Goods ExAutos UNCH    0.2    0.2	1.4</p>
<p>The department reported October price indexes (1990 base year equals 100) of 108.1 for imports, and 108.4 for exports.</p>
</text>
